;; Eve-in-cohost unit 6 (doc/eve-cohost/UNIT6-DESIGN.md section 8.2): cohost's
;; jank boot and battery with Eve's core completion loaded into the same
;; process -- the "two type layers in one jank process" question step 2 raises.
;; cohost's namespaces load first (as bb boot:jank loads them); then
;; eve.host-completion, which interns deftype, defprotocol, ... into
;; clojure.core and re-roots =, hash, type, defn, fn, let, case, deref, ...
;; for every namespace compiled after it; then cohost.run/-main boots the stock
;; core and runs the battery and libraries, all of which compile after it.
;;
;;   LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 jank --module-path <aot-dir>:src:<bb classpath jank> \
;;     run dev/u6/boot_with_completion.jank
;;
;; No Eve atom, region or value is used: only the completion is loaded.
(require 'cohost.run)
(require 'eve.host-completion)
(println "EVE-COMPLETION-LOADED")
(apply cohost.run/-main (or *command-line-args* ()))
